<title>HUNGARY: IEB requests to requalify its shares.</title>
<headline>IEB requests to requalify its shares.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inter-Europa Bank said on Wednesday it was requesting the requalification of its shares to the &quot;listed A&quot; category of the Budapest Stock Exchange from the &quot;listed B&quot; where they are traded now.</p>
<p>The bank lodged its request in a letter dated March 24, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Differences between the &quot;listed A&quot; and &quot;listed B&quot; categories of the Hungarian bourse include stricter obligations on providing information.</p>
<p>Inter-Europa Bank is member of Italy's Gruppo Bancario San Paolo.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
